<form display="yes">
<congress display="yes">119th CONGRESS</congress><session display="yes">2d Session</session><legis-num display="yes">S. 5123</legis-num><current-chamber display="no">IN THE SENATE OF THE UNITED STATES</current-chamber><legis-type display="yes">AN ACT</legis-type><official-title display="yes">To amend title 36, United States Code, to designate July 20 as Lunar Landing Day.</official-title></form><legis-body style="OLC" display-enacting-clause="yes-display-enacting-clause"><section id="S1" section-type="section-one" commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline"><enum>1.</enum><header display-inline="yes-display-inline">Short title</header><text display-inline="no-display-inline">This Act may be cited as the <quote><short-title>Lunar Landing Day Act</short-title></quote>.</text></section><section commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id975cd1cf32214af292113e7173baf021" section-type="subsequent-section"><enum>2.</enum><header display-inline="yes-display-inline">Designation</header><subsection id="id2d2cde265b784912a7104add95358ee6" commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline"><enum>(a)</enum><header display-inline="yes-display-inline">In general</header><text display-inline="yes-display-inline"><external-xref legal-doc="usc-chapter" parsable-cite="usc-chapter/36/1">Chapter 1</external-xref> of title 36, United States Code, is amended—</text><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="ida86820b20ea94783b446c75ca499b0e8"><enum>(1)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by redesignating sections 106 through 115 as sections 107 through 116, respectively;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id1ffce71131c24602abf4b3798b80cfd7"><enum>(2)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by moving section 147 so as to appear after section 105 and by redesignating such section 147 as section 106;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id5eca7ed553a54b91b32ba07f6328fe37"><enum>(3)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by redesignating the second section designated as section 106 and sections 107 through 116 as sections 107 through 116, respectively;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id0345a271cc3640f5b78a09ab7d896410"><enum>(4)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by redesignating the second section designated as 116 and section 117 as sections 118 and 119, respectively;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id18ced5b4aa3a47e9bee5de39d4407e01"><enum>(5)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by moving section 146 so as to appear after section 119, as so redesignated, and by redesignating such section 146 as section 120;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="idd9c54b8fe13e4b0b80c321ede87ef628"><enum>(6)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by redesignating the second section designated as section 118, the second section designated as section 119, and sections 120 through 135 as sections 121 through 138, respectively;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="ida643094667d54b2589d7d9a808838d0b"><enum>(7)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by moving section 144 so as to appear after section 138, as so redesignated, and by redesignating such section 144 as section 139;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="idf9708a02952547a095d4e889e5ed2908"><enum>(8)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by redesignating the second section designated as section 136, the second section designated as section 137, the second section designated as section 138, the second section designated as section 139, and sections 140 and 141 as sections 140 through 145, respectively;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id3081a7e62846494ca0ce7d1ea942470e"><enum>(9)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by moving section 148 so as to appear after section 145, as so redesignated, and by redesignating such section 148 as section 146;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id919de9b7653446b3b12801a93f315e28"><enum>(10)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by moving the second section designated as section 145 so as to appear after section 146, as so redesignated, and by redesignating such section 145 as section 147;</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id987c5b8dcf5944b195535f6e2853109c"><enum>(11)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by redesignating the second section designated as section 142 and the second section designated as section 143 as sections 148 and 149, respectively; and</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id0bb32999c60e408eaf0c04b5c49fc141"><enum>(12)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">by inserting after section 116, as so redesignated, the following:</text><quoted-block style="USC" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="idc82266248d3b4c699e03fd054c50b7aa"><section id="id3d77e69d14cf41aba016a5152e1f4b48" commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" section-type="subsequent-section"><enum>117.</enum><header display-inline="yes-display-inline">Lunar Landing Day</header><subsection id="iddc28b0def01e4b7f8d3ab47422ff87db" commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline"><enum>(a)</enum><header display-inline="yes-display-inline">Designation</header><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">July 20 is Lunar Landing Day.</text></subsection><subsection id="id86e3efd55a5c49a384e1a7057bbe59e6" commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline"><enum>(b)</enum><header display-inline="yes-display-inline">Recognition</header><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">All private citizens, organizations, and Federal, State, and local governmental and legislative entities are encouraged to recognize Lunar Landing Day through proclamations, activities, and educational efforts—</text><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="idb62d075110984a91b45e3ee786068e99"><enum>(1)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">commemorating the first successful landing of humans on the Moon on July 20, 1969; and</text></paragraph><paragraph commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id2763f9d5b75a44f0a796d2fb39c19ecd"><enum>(2)</enum><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">inspiring the continued leadership of the United States in space exploration and science.</text></paragraph></subsection></section><after-quoted-block display="yes">.</after-quoted-block></quoted-block></paragraph></subsection><subsection id="idd18841105c8b4dbc8ceea046f962304c" commented="no" display-inline="no-display-inline"><enum>(b)</enum><header display-inline="yes-display-inline">Technical and conforming amendment</header><text display-inline="yes-display-inline">The table of sections for <external-xref legal-doc="usc-chapter" parsable-cite="usc-chapter/36/1">chapter 1</external-xref> of title 36, United States Code, is amended by striking the items relating to sections 101 through 148 and inserting the following:</text><quoted-block style="OLC" display-inline="no-display-inline" id="id3db40e0c63f4439d89dd3e60e9d2b2ad"><toc><toc-entry level="section" bold="off">101. American Heart Month.</toc-entry><toc-entry level="section" bold="off">102. Asian/Pacific American Heritage Month.</toc-entry><toc-entry level="section" bold="off">103. Cancer Control Month.</toc-entry><toc-entry level="section" bold="off">104. Carl Garner Federal Lands Cleanup Day.</toc-entry><toc-entry level="section" bold="off">105. Child Health Day.</toc-entry><toc-entry level="section" bold="off">106. Choose Respect Day.</toc-entry><toc-entry level="section" bold="off">107. Constitu